#34 round 1:
- blocking [correctness] crates/shed-server/src/lib.rs:738: the read-only check resolves the terminal with `target()`, which prefers a `terminal` field over `name`, but `resize` (ResizeParams has no `terminal` alias, so an extra `terminal` key is ignored) acts on `name`. A read-only client can resize a terminal it marked read-only by sending `{"name":"w","terminal":"<any other terminal>"}`.
  Proof: run
  ```
  python3 -I t2.py  (conn A: terminal.readonly{terminal:w}; A: resize{name:w, terminal:free, rows:7, cols:33}; conn B: send "stty size", read w)
  ```
  ```
  {"id":2,"result":{}}                      <- terminal.readonly w
  {"id":3,"result":{}}                      <- resize of w by the read-only connection: accepted
  {"text":"sh-3.2$ stty size\n7 33\nsh-3.2$"}  <- w really is 7x33
  ```
  Required by the issue: "a terminal can be marked `readonly` for a given client, and input from such a client is refused" and the PR's own claim that `resize` to it "fails with READONLY". Without the extra key the same call returns `READONLY: w` (-32006).


