#42 round 2:
- blocking [correctness] crates/shed-server/src/events.rs:93: a subscriber with `since` beyond the current seq (e.g. a client resuming with its old last seq against a restarted server, seq back at 0) silently loses every new event up to that seq. `subscribe` sets the cursor to `since` (`s.max(oldest)`), and `take()` only lowers it when the log is non-empty (`events.back().map_or(cursor, ..)`), so on an empty log the cursor stays at `since` and `emit`s numbered <= since are skipped. The base (`origin/staging:crates/shed-server/src/events.rs`, `subscribe`/`emit_as`) sent every new event to the subscriber regardless of `since`. This is a client-visible change on the socket protocol.
  Proof: run
  ```
  # scratch checkout of the head with this test added to events.rs tests:
  #   let mut events = Events::default();
  #   let mut sub = events.subscribe(EventsParams { labels: Labels::new(), since: Some(5) });
  #   assert!(sub.take().is_empty());
  #   for _ in 0..3 { events.emit("t", &Labels::new(), EventKind::Started); }
  #   assert_eq!(sub.take().len(), 3);
  CARGO_TARGET_DIR="$HERDSMAN_SCRATCH_TARGET/target" cargo test -q -p shed-server --lib since_beyond
  ```
  ```
  thread 'events::tests::since_beyond_seq_still_gets_new_events' panicked at crates/shed-server/src/events.rs:172:9:
  assertion `left == right` failed
    left: 0
   right: 3
  test result: FAILED. 0 passed; 1 failed
  ```
  Required: > "All existing tests pass. The CLI and socket protocol (`shed-proto`) don't change for clients." Fix: clamp the cursor to `self.seq` in `subscribe` (`s.max(oldest).min(self.seq)`), and add that test.


